{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nRunning `review_plan` through the deployed MCP server, the agentic VERIFY step fails every time\nwith an asyncio error, so findings that would be confirmed or dismissed by verification stay\n`indeterminate` and the verdict can never reach a signed PASS.\n\n    \"verify_failed\": true,\n    \"verify_error\": \"step 'review@then/prerequisite_verify' failed: This event loop is already running\"\n    \"verify_requests\": 0\n    counts: {blocking: 0, advisory_surfaced: 1, indeterminate: 4}\n\n## Why this is P1\n\nA plan-review attestation is what the CLAIM GATE consumes. If the verify pass cannot run inside\nthe MCP server, then `review_plan` via MCP cannot produce a signed PASS — so the mandated\n'route tracker ops through the MCP server' path can never satisfy the claim gate, and every agent\nusing it must fall back to the local CLI. That is the same class of outcome as\n`fatherly-incoherent-mare`, reached by a different mechanism.\n\n## Mechanism (hypothesis — NOT yet proven, deliberately)\n\n`This event loop is already running` is the signature of synchronous `asyncio.run()` (or\n`loop.run_until_complete`) being called from inside an already-running loop. The MCP server is an\nASGI application, so every tool call executes inside a live event loop; a verify step that\nspawns its own loop works under the CLI (no loop running) and fails under MCP. That would explain\nwhy this is invisible locally — the exact asymmetry that hid `facial-lunar-urson` too.\n\nI have NOT confirmed the call site. Whoever picks this up should find where the verify step\nenters async code and check it uses `await`/`anyio.from_thread` rather than starting a loop.\n\n## Evidence\n\nObserved live against `rebar-mcp-8e2e3893e904-8093`, the deployed container, calling\n`review_plan` on `d43e-c24f-dd39-44e9`. The LLM leg itself is HEALTHY — this is not the Bedrock\nbug (that is fixed and verified): `llm_ran: true`, `llm_calls: 27`, `llm_ms: 4932`,\n`llm_error: null`. Only the verify step fails.\n\n`verify_requests: 0` is worth noting: the counter says zero requests were made, consistent with\nthe step dying before issuing any.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `review_plan` through the deployed MCP server completes its verify pass —\n      `verify_failed` is false and `verify_requests` > 0 when findings need verification.\n- [x] The root cause is identified as a specific call site, not 'an async problem'.\n- [x] A regression test exercises the verify step from inside a RUNNING event loop, so a fix\n      cannot regress the moment it is only tested from the CLI.\n- [x] LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE: a `review_plan` call through\n      `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` returning a verdict with a completed verify\n      pass, recorded in a ticket comment.\n\n## Found by\n\nLive-validating the Bedrock provider fix (`facial-lunar-urson`). The Bedrock error is gone; this\nwas underneath it."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787902497475682001,"uuid":"7019210c-ed1b-40f8-97d9-6fa0517198e0"}